  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Consider the equation $2\\cos x+\\sin x=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $2\\cos x+\\sin x=B\\cos(x-\\theta)$, where $B>0$ and $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$. Show that $B=\\sqrt5$ and $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$B=\\sqrt5$, $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}B\\cos(x-\\theta)&=B\\cos x\\cos\\theta+B\\sin x\\sin\\theta\\\\B\\cos\\theta&=2\\\\B\\sin\\theta&=1\\\\B^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)&=2^2+1^2\\\\B^2&=5\\\\B&=\\sqrt5\\quad(B>0)\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{B\\sin\\theta}{B\\cos\\theta}=\\frac12\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\end{aligned}$$\nBoth $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$ are positive, so $\\theta$ is in quadrant I.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find, correct to the nearest minute where necessary, the solutions of the equation, for $0^\\circ\\leq x\\leq360^\\circ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=90^\\circ$ or $x\\approx323^\\circ8'$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt5\\cos(x-\\theta)&=1\\\\\\cos(x-\\theta)&=\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\approx26^\\circ34'\\end{aligned}$$\nLet $\\beta=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\right)=90^\\circ-\\theta$. Since $-\\theta\\leq x-\\theta\\leq360^\\circ-\\theta$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}x-\\theta&=\\beta,\\ 360^\\circ-\\beta\\\\x&=\\theta+\\beta,\\ \\theta+360^\\circ-\\beta\\\\x&=90^\\circ,\\ 270^\\circ+2\\theta\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $x=90^\\circ$ or $x\\approx323^\\circ8'$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
